From 07be7db9f2de53f23b9b6bcf562fff5956a7db1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pugant <pugant@localhost>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 17:45:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 16/19] vulkan: track unsynchronized accesses per buffer (A6-S2
 / W6-4)

Replace the flat unsynced_nodes_written/read tensor lists with a
per-buffer tracker (ggml-vulkan-sync.hpp). The hazard test only ever
compares accesses inside the same device buffer, so grouping regions by
buffer keeps every sync decision identical while the scan cost no longer
grows with the accesses tracked for the other buffers (the weight-buffer
read list no longer taxes every destination check).

The sync decision is proven identical to the previous semantics by
tests/test-vk-sync-tracker.cpp: a reference implementation of the old
flat-list predicate runs in lockstep over randomized node-group
sequences (20 seeds x 2000 groups, dst + up to 4 srcs each), plus
pattern tests for RAW/WAR/WAW per buffer, cross-buffer independence,
adjacent/disjoint ranges and the zero-size edges of the original
strict-inequality predicate.

Prerequisite for the scoped barriers of A6-S1 (follow-up commit).

Co-Authored-By: GLM by z.ai
